First add the fractions eaten.
$\begin{align*}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\frac{1}{10}+\frac{3}{10}+\frac{2}{10}\\&=\frac{6}{10}\end{align*}$
Subtract from the whole pizza, keeping tenths until the final answer.
$\begin{align*}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\frac{10}{10}-\frac{6}{10}\\&=\frac{4}{10}\\&=\frac{2}{5}\end{align*}$
The unshaded sectors show the fraction left.
